{"run_id": "20260814T133731-hepkg-48442", "qid": "gen-retrieval-0227a4f8", "repeat": 0, "system": "hepkg", "config_hash": "9f0ca51b332d", "git_sha": "feb9060-dirty", "question": "Which analyses measured CP-violating anomalous coupling c~_w/Lambda^2 constraint from M(WZ) tail?", "shape": "set", "split": "dev", "needs": ["sql"], "difficulty": "hard", "answer": {"text": "The analysis reported in the paper with arXiv ID [2110.11231](https://arxiv.org/abs/2110.11231) measured the CP-violating anomalous coupling \\( c~_w/\\Lambda^2 \\) constraint from the \\( M(WZ) \\) tail. Here are some key details from the paper:\n\n### Background Estimation Methods\n- **Direct simulation-based background estimate**: Fixed normalization, no control region (CR) fit.\n- **MC-based prediction with free-floating normalization**: Constrained via a dedicated control region in the combined fit.\n- **Tight-to-loose data-driven nonprompt-lepton estimation method**.\n\n### Event Regions\n- **Signal Region (SR^WZ)**: On-shell WZ selection.\n- **Control Region (CR-conv)**: Photon conversion.\n- **Control Region (CR-ZZ)**: ZZ selection.\n- **Control Region (CR-ttZ)**: ttZ/tZq selection.\n\n### Model Parameters\n- **\\( c_b/\\Lambda^2 \\)**: CP-conserving WWZ aTGC coefficient.\n- **\\( c_w/\\Lambda^2 \\)**: CP-conserving WWZ aTGC coefficient.\n- **\\( c_www/\\Lambda^2 \\)**: CP-conserving WWZ aTGC coefficient.\n- **\\( c~_w/\\Lambda^2 \\)**: CP-violating WWZ aTGC coefficient.\n- **\\( c~_www/\\Lambda^2 \\)**: CP-violating WWZ aTGC coefficient.\n\n### Selection Requirements\n- **Lepton Mass and Momentum**: \\( 60 < M(lZ1, lZ2) < 120 \\) GeV.\n- **B-jet Tagging**: DeepCSV tight working point (~0.1% mistag, 40-60% b-tag efficiency).\n- **Invariant Mass**: \\( M(lZ1, lZ2, lW) > 100 \\) GeV.\n- **Charge Consistency**: Consistency required among three independent electron charge measurements.\n- **Lepton Multiplicity**: Exactly three tight light leptons with at least one opposite-sign same-flavor (OSSF) pair.\n- **Neutrino Assumptions**: Longitudinal momentum and mass of neutrino assumed zero in computation of \\( M(WZ) \\).\n- **Track Curvature**: Measured track curvature relative uncertainty < 20%.\n- **Minimum Invariant Mass**: \\( \\min(M(l, l')) > 4 \\) GeV for any lepton pair.\n- **Neutrino Momentum**: Neutrino \\( p_z \\) solved from \\( p_T^{\\text{miss}} \\) by fixing reconstructed W mass to world-average \\( m_W \\), neutrino assumed massless.\n- **Lepton Kinematics**: \\( p_T > 25 \\) GeV, \\( |\\eta| < 2.5 \\), plus noise-rejection identification criteria.\n- **Additional Lepton Kinematics**: \\( p_T > 5 \\) GeV, \\( |\\eta| < 2.4 \\) and \\( p_T > 7 \\) GeV, \\( |\\eta| < 2.5 \\).\n- **Lepton Transverse Momenta**: \\( p_T(lZ1) > 25 \\) GeV, \\( p_T(lZ2) > 10 \\) GeV, \\( p_T(lW) > 25 \\) GeV.\n\nThis analysis provides a comprehensive study of the CP-violating anomalous coupling \\( c~_w/\\Lambda^2 \\) using the \\( M(WZ) \\) tail, with detailed background estimation and selection criteria.\n\n<tool_call>\n{\"name\": \"answer\", \"arguments\": {\"text\": \"The analysis", "answered": true, "papers": ["2001.06899", "2004.01678", "2004.04545", "2004.14060", "2006.05880", "2007.02873", "2008.05928", "2009.04363", "2009.14537", "2010.14293", "2011.07812", "2012.01581", "2012.03799", "2012.08600", "2102.01444", "2103.04956", "2103.06956", "2106.01676", "2106.14246", "2107.12553", "2109.13808", "2110.11231", "2111.08340", "2112.00895", "2112.03161", "2201.11585", "2202.08676", "2205.05120", "2206.09466", "2207.00348", "2208.12095", "2209.07327", "2211.08028", "2302.05225", "2304.08962", "2307.01094", "2308.02285", "2309.14442", "2312.04450", "2401.05299", "2401.07090", "2402.08486", "2403.01556", "2404.06204", "2405.18661", "2407.10549", "2408.03744", "2503.19420", "2504.13081", "2506.13565", "2508.13900", "2509.22535", "2510.07527", "2511.11853", "2602.18611", "2604.21670", "2604.27044", "2605.14245"], "value": null, "steps": [{"round": 1, "tool": "search", "args": {"text": "CP-violating anomalous coupling c~_w/Lambda^2", "kind": "observable"}, "rows": 31, "error": null, "seconds": 0.19}, {"round": 2, "tool": "subjects_of", "args": {"predicate": "result_measures_observable", "object_set": "set_1"}, "rows": 48, "error": null, "seconds": 0.04}, {"round": 3, "tool": "papers_of", "args": {"entity_ids": ["hepkg:observable:atgc-cw-tilde-observable"]}, "rows": 1, "error": null, "seconds": 0.009}, {"round": 4, "tool": "contents_of", "args": {"paper_ids": ["2110.11231"]}, "rows": 159, "error": null, "seconds": 1.559}], "sets": {"set_1": ["hepkg:observable:AC_llbar", "hepkg:observable:AC_ttbar", "hepkg:observable:acrel-inclusive", "hepkg:observable:atgc-cb-observable", "hepkg:observable:atgc-cw-observable", "hepkg:observable:atgc-cw-tilde-observable", "hepkg:observable:atgc-cwww-observable", "hepkg:observable:atgc-cwww-tilde-observable", "hepkg:observable:coupling_e_tau", "hepkg:observable:coupling_modifier_ratio", "hepkg:observable:coupling_mu_tau", "hepkg:observable:coupling_symmetry_leptonquark", "hepkg:observable:coupling_symmetry_updown", "hepkg:observable:fit_basis_linear_no_dihiggs", "hepkg:observable:fit_basis_linear_quadratic", "hepkg:observable:fit_basis_linear_with_dihiggs", "hepkg:observable:higgs_self_coupling_modifier", "hepkg:observable:individual_warsaw_coeff_constraints", "hepkg:observable:kappa-lambda", "hepkg:observable:rc-ratio-inclusive", "hepkg:observable:scale_factor_c", "hepkg:observable:sigma-wc-particle-inclusive", "hepkg:observable:sigma-wc-parton-inclusive", "hepkg:observable:smeft_wilson_coefficient", "hepkg:observable:tan_alpha", "hepkg:observable:ttw-minus-xsec", "hepkg:observable:ttw-plus-xsec", "hepkg:observable:w-polarization-flr", "hepkg:observable:xsec-br-tchislepsnu", "hepkg:observable:xsec-br-tchiww", "hepkg:observable:xsec-br-tchiwz"]}, "entity_ids": ["hepkg:background:nonprompt-lepton", "hepkg:background:ttz-tzq", "hepkg:background:vh", "hepkg:background:vvv", "hepkg:background:wz-ewk", "hep