{"run_id": "20260814T133731-hepkg-48442", "qid": "gen-retrieval-03901cf3", "repeat": 0, "system": "hepkg", "config_hash": "9f0ca51b332d", "git_sha": "feb9060-dirty", "question": "Which analyses estimate a background using Background normalization varied within theoretical cross section uncertainties?", "shape": "set", "split": "dev", "needs": ["sql"], "difficulty": "hard", "answer": {"text": "The following analyses estimate a background using methods related to \"Background normalization varied within theoretical cross section uncertainties\":\n\n- **2004.14060**: Estimates $Z\\to\\nu\\bar{\\nu}$ + heavy-flavour jets, $t\\bar{t}$, and $W$+jets backgrounds.\n- **2007.02873**: Estimates Z+jets background.\n- **2010.14293**: Estimates Z+jets and W+jets backgrounds.\n- **2012.03799**: Estimates $t\\bar{t}$, W+jets, and Z+jets backgrounds.\n- **2102.01444**: Estimates $t\\bar{t}$ and Z+jets backgrounds.\n- **2106.01676**: Uses Z+jets MC sample, estimates SM WZ, $t\\bar{t}$, and Z+jets (FNP-lepton) backgrounds.\n- **2109.13808**: Estimates Drell-Yan Z/gamma*+jets and non-resonant WW diboson backgrounds.\n- **2110.11231**: Estimates VVV triboson background.\n- **2202.08676**: Estimates WZ irreducible background.\n- **2208.12095**: Estimates $W{+}\\text{jets}$ and $Z{+}\\text{jets}$ backgrounds.\n- **2211.08028**: Estimates $t t̄$, W+jets, and Z+jets backgrounds.\n- **2308.02285**: Estimates top quark-antiquark (ttbar) background.\n\nThese analyses use various methods for background estimation, including control-region-based normalisation, direct MC simulation, and theoretical cross-section predictions. For more detailed information on the specific methods used in each analysis, please refer to the respective papers.\n\nAnswered from the graph, which contains the relevant information.", "answered": true, "papers": ["2001.06899", "2004.04545", "2004.14060", "2006.05880", "2007.02873", "2008.05928", "2009.04363", "2009.14537", "2010.14293", "2011.07812", "2012.03799", "2102.0